project: heapless
repo: rust-embedded/heapless
audited_path: src/
baseline:
  tag: v0.9.1
  commit: 19188229ac2b76fc91ad79f57dee01fa362a1e15
  date: 2025-08-20
size:
  total_lines: 17537
  code_lines: 10339
  unsafe: 254
build:
  toolchain: stable 1.99.1, aarch64 Linux container; nightly-2026-10-01 with Miri
    for soundness reproducers
  features:
  - alloc
  - defmt
  - mpmc_large
  - portable-atomic-critical-section
  - serde
  - ufmt
  - bytes
  system_libraries: []
  lockfile: Tag has no Cargo.lock. Generated with `cargo generate-lockfile` (kept
    at base/Cargo.lock), nothing pinned. Fresh resolve took later bytes, serde, defmt
    and portable-atomic, but the reproducers link only hash32 0.3.1, byteorder and
    stable_deref_trait, plus portable-atomic and critical-section for the pool ones,
    and none of the symptoms depend on them. --publish-time exists on nightly cargo
    and was not needed. Each repro folder keeps its own Cargo.lock.
  build_result: Builds. `cargo build --features=alloc,defmt,mpmc_large,portable-atomic-critical-section,serde,ufmt,bytes`
  test_result: '`cargo test --no-fail-fast --features=<same>`: unit 220 pass, tests/cpass
    1 pass, tests/tsan 8 pass, doctests 184 pass, 0 failures, but only with `TMPDIR=/work/tmp`.
    With the default TMPDIR, doctests show 2 pass and 182 fail, all ''Couldn''t run
    the test: Permission denied'', because /tmp in the sandbox is noexec. That is
    the environment, not the crate.'
  notes: Container is aarch64, so build.rs skips the LL/SC probe and pool uses the
    CAS path, which needs portable-atomic on 64-bit. The upstream Miri suite, TSan
    job and cfail/ were not run. Reproducers must not use a target dir under /tmp,
    which is noexec. Fix trees are in fixes/<sha8>; each repro has fix/run.sh and
    fix/output.txt, where exit non-zero means the bug was not demonstrated.
ai_policy: 'none found. Checked at main tip: README.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, .github/
  (bors.toml, workflows). No CONTRIBUTING, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/ or PR template
  exists. Not a claim that the project has no policy.'
bugs:
- id: heapless-6
  kind: wrong-behavior
  summary: IndexMap::truncate clears index slots of removed entries without repairing
    probe chains, so keys still in the map cannot be found.
  location:
  - src/index_map.rs:1269
  - src/index_map.rs:1274
  confirmed_at_baseline: reproduced
  match_rule: Names that IndexMap::truncate sets index slots to None with no backward
    shift or rebuild, breaking robin-hood probing so surviving keys become unreachable
    through lookup.
  caveat: ''
- id: heapless-11
  kind: crash-from-input
  summary: IndexMap accepts any power-of-two N although Pos holds a 16-bit index,
    so maps above 65536 entries overflow in Pos::new, lose keys, and can hang in remove.
  location:
  - src/index_map.rs:104
  - src/index_map.rs:115
  - src/index_map.rs:285
  - src/index_map.rs:735
  confirmed_at_baseline: reproduced
  match_rule: Names that IndexMap's const checks put no upper bound on N while Pos
    stores the index in 16 bits, so with N above 65536 positions overflow or truncate.
    A finding of the Pos::new overflow panic, of lost lookups or of remove_found never
    terminating all match if tied to that limit.
  caveat: 'Added while building the key, split out of the candidate for 2e73f81, so
    it shares a fix commit with heapless-5 and is a different defect in the same area.
    The panic is debug-only and needs N > 65536. The remove hang is a symptom of this
    bug and is not claimed as a separate resource-exhaustion bug: it is a step, not
    a growth curve.'
- id: heapless-12
  kind: wrong-behavior
  summary: spsc len() computes (tail - head + N) % N with a wrapping add, which wraps
    when N is close to usize::MAX, so it undercounts and iter() yields too few items.
  location:
  - src/spsc.rs:198
  - src/spsc.rs:204
  confirmed_at_baseline: reproduced
  match_rule: Names that spsc len's wrapping_add of N can wrap for N near usize::MAX
    and return a wrong length.
  caveat: 'Contrived: only a zero-sized T allows such an N. Upstream fixed it incidentally,
    while removing the modulo. The CHANGELOG''s ''panic in len'' for N == usize::MAX
    is a different failure, introduced by d02bc5e2 after the tag and not present here.'
- id: heapless-13
  kind: crash-from-input
  summary: spsc iterators compute head + index unchecked, which overflows and panics
    in debug when N exceeds usize::MAX/2 and head is high.
  location:
  - src/spsc.rs:626
  - src/spsc.rs:643
  - src/spsc.rs:659
  - src/spsc.rs:674
  confirmed_at_baseline: read
  match_rule: Names the unchecked addition of head and index in spsc Iter or IterMut,
    overflowing when N exceeds usize::MAX/2.
  caveat: 'Contrived: zero-sized T only. The reproducer sets private fields, which
    is why this is read and not reproduced, and it does not count toward the key.'
